# Test: `withdraw` is three commands, one per form, each stating its own grammar
# VALIDATES: AC-11 -- withdraw tag, withdraw id and withdraw all each carry their
#            own usage line, and withdraw alone lists them as subcommands
# PREVENTS: four tail grammars behind one handler, which no model can state and
#           no operator can discover from help
#
# The line each form states is the one the MODEL renders. The tag value is
# optional, because the handler defaults it to "*", which the authored prose got
# wrong. `withdraw all` takes no tail: it carried a selector filter until
# 2026-08-31, when the peer prefix replaced it so one scope reaches all three
# forms rather than one.
#
# Each form is reachable at two paths, bare and under `peer <selector>`, the same
# as the announce forms.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze withdraw help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze withdraw <command> [options]
expect=stderr:contains=Commands
expect=stderr:contains=tag
expect=stderr:contains=id
expect=stderr:contains=all
reject=stderr:pattern=withdraw tag <key> <value\|\*>

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze withdraw tag help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze withdraw tag <key> [value <value>]

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze withdraw id help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze withdraw id <id>

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze withdraw all help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze withdraw all
reject=stderr:pattern=withdraw all \[selector

cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze peer withdraw tag help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze peer <selector> withdraw tag <key> [value <value>]

cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze peer withdraw id help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze peer <selector> withdraw id <id>

cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze peer withdraw all help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze peer <selector> withdraw all
